1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:04,120
Let's dive straight in with visiting cambridge's architecturally stunning colleges.
先从参观剑桥建筑上令人惊叹的学院开始吧。

2
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:11,240
The famous university was founded in 1209 making cambridge the second oldest university in the english speaking world.
作者介绍，这所著名大学创立于一二〇九年，是英语世界中历史第二悠久的大学。

3
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:18,394
An interesting fact is that affiliates of the university of cambridge have been awarded more nobel prizes than any other institution.
作者提到一个有趣的说法：剑桥大学相关人士获得的诺贝尔奖，比其他任何机构的都多。

4
00:00:18,394 --> 00:00:24,296
Rather than being one central campus the university is made up of 31 autonomous colleges.
这所大学并非只有一个集中式校园，而是由三十一所自治学院组成。

5
00:00:24,296 --> 00:00:29,064
Students become a member of one of these colleges where they live eat and socialise.
学生会成为其中一所学院的成员，在那里居住、吃饭和社交。

6
00:00:29,064 --> 00:00:34,040
And most colleges even have their own sports team which compete against each other in intercollegiate cuppers.
大多数学院甚至有自己的运动队，会在学院间的杯赛中相互竞技。

7
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:40,920
You can visit many of these colleges some for a reasonable admission fee which will allow you to stroll around the impressive grounds.
作者说，许多学院可供参观，有些收取合理的门票费，游客可以在壮观的院落里漫步。

8
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:45,588
And see parts of the colleges that you would otherwise miss if you only viewed them from the outside.
还能看到学院内部的一些区域；如果只从外面看，就会错过这些地方。

9
00:00:45,588 --> 00:00:51,695
If there are any colleges you would like to visit in particular then check in advance to make sure they are accepting visitors.
如果你特别想参观某几所学院，就提前确认它们是否接待游客。

10
00:00:51,695 --> 00:00:55,944
At the time of our visit in july 2021 they were still closed to the public.
作者在二〇二一年七月到访时，那些学院仍然不对公众开放。

11
00:00:55,944 --> 00:01:02,449
So if you do have your heart set on going inside one of these colleges make sure you check their website before booking your trip.
所以，如果你确实非常想走进某所学院，预订旅行前一定先查阅它的网站。

12
00:01:02,449 --> 00:01:07,339
You will also need to be aware of exam periods that could mean colleges are closed.
你还需要留意考试期间，因为那可能意味着学院会关闭。

13
00:01:07,339 --> 00:01:13,080
From researching best colleges to visit in cambridge I've pulled together this list of recommended colleges to get you started.
在研究剑桥最值得参观的学院后，我整理了这份推荐清单，供你开始做计划。

14
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:19,503
However when we visited even though many colleges were closed king's college chapel had reopened to visitors.
不过，我们去的时候，虽然许多学院关闭了，国王学院礼拜堂已经重新向游客开放。

15
00:01:19,503 --> 00:01:26,093
We strolled the beautifully manicured grounds where the pathways were lined with what I think are called echiums I'm not sure.
我们在修剪整齐的院落里散步，小径两旁种着我想应该叫蓝蓟的植物，不过我也不确定。

16
00:01:26,093 --> 00:01:35,320
And once we reach the river the sea of wildflowers beautifully framed the impressive college buildings you can also go inside the chapel.
等我们走到河边，一大片野花把壮观的学院建筑衬托得格外好看。你也可以走进礼拜堂参观。

17
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:46,444
Construction of the chapel began in 1446 by Henry vi and was completed in 1515 when the country lived under the rule of Henry viii.
据作者介绍，礼拜堂在亨利六世时期于一四四六年开始建造，到一五一五年、亨利八世统治时竣工。

18
00:01:46,444 --> 00:01:55,640
When you head in look all the way up to see the incredible largest fan vaulted ceiling in the world and admire the enormous medieval stained glass windows.
走进去后，抬头一直往上看，作者称那里有世界上最大的扇形拱顶，令人惊叹。再欣赏那些巨大的中世纪彩色玻璃窗。

19
00:01:56,680 --> 00:02:00,520
If you would like to hear the king's college choir perform then you could attend evensong.
如果想听国王学院唱诗班演唱，你可以参加晚祷礼拜。

20
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:04,600
So make sure you check the king's college website for information on upcoming services.
所以，一定查看国王学院网站，了解接下来礼拜活动的信息。

21
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:10,882
Number two on our list is to go on a walking tour.
我们清单上的第二项，是参加步行导览。

22
00:02:10,882 --> 00:02:14,912
Walking tours give you a great opportunity to learn more about the city and its colleges.
步行导览让你有很好的机会，更深入了解这座城市及其学院。

23
00:02:14,912 --> 00:02:21,198
And what better way to learn more about a city famous for its university than to take a guided tour with a student.
要了解一座以大学闻名的城市，还有什么方式比跟着学生参加导览更合适呢？

24
00:02:21,198 --> 00:02:29,453
History and facts combined with personal stories and experiences of somebody who does actually live and study in cambridge really helped add to our appreciation for the city.
历史和事实，加上真正在剑桥生活、学习的人分享的亲身故事和经历，确实让我们更加懂得欣赏这座城市。

25
00:02:29,453 --> 00:02:35,488
I'll link the tour company we used in the description below but there are plenty of other different types of tours for you to choose from.
我会在下方说明栏放上我们所选导览公司的链接。不过，还有很多其他不同类型的导览可供选择。

26
00:02:35,488 --> 00:02:39,420
So I'll also include links to the relevant pages on the visit cambridge website.
因此，我也会附上 Visit Cambridge 网站相关页面的链接。

27
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:42,280
If you're wondering whether or not a walking tour is worth it.
如果你在想，步行导览究竟值不值得参加，

28
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:48,307
I would say that if you would like to hear more about the history and listen to some interesting anecdotes then yes it is worth it.
我的看法是，如果你想多了解历史、听一些有趣的轶事，那么确实值得。

29
00:02:48,307 --> 00:02:52,644
However if you just want to see the main sights and get a feel for the place.
但如果你只是想看主要景点，感受一下这座城市的氛围，

30
00:02:52,644 --> 00:02:59,320
Then as cambridge is a small and very pedestrian friendly city then with a bit of research I think you could devise your own walking tour.
剑桥是一座小巧、很适合步行的城市，所以我觉得，稍做研究，你也能设计自己的步行路线。
